{"title":"Maximum-minimum theorem","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>The <b>Maximum-minimum theorem</b> is a result about continous functions that deals with a property of intervals rather than that of the function itself.\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Statement\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Statement</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Proof\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Proof</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#References\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">References</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Statement\">Statement</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Maximum-minimum_theorem&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Statement\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/c/67c320754a36aaec178e61f04bfcbac41c0bf675.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f:[a,b]\\rightarrow\\mathbb{R}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"102\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> be continous on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/c/8ecbd1ba3da8f2adef66a63f2ab32c47e63fa734.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[a,b]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Then, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> has an <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Extrema\" title=\"Extrema\">absolute maximum</a> and an <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Extrema\" title=\"Extrema\">absolute minimum</a> on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/c/8ecbd1ba3da8f2adef66a63f2ab32c47e63fa734.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[a,b]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Proof\">Proof</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Maximum-minimum_theorem&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Proof\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We will first show that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> is bounded on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/c/8ecbd1ba3da8f2adef66a63f2ab32c47e63fa734.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[a,b]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" />...(1)\n</p><p>Assume if possible <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/c/b8c9046f7b254367d38a007ef5fbf6780b8434da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\forall n\\in\\mathbb{N}\\exists x_n\\in [a,b]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"141\" height=\"18\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/7/db7ca9723e13800d87f961e8bdc6ceec346da163.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x_n)&gt;n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"79\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>As <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/c/8ecbd1ba3da8f2adef66a63f2ab32c47e63fa734.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[a,b]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> is bounded, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/7/c17dd0a72cb06528993d591975faf08cf6288c63.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left\\langle  x_n\\right\\rangle$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"32\" height=\"19\" /> is bounded.\n</p><p>By the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Bolzano-Weierstrass_theorem\" title=\"Bolzano-Weierstrass theorem\">Bolzano-Weierstrass theorem</a>, there exists a sunsequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/2/3d242fcfc8b8d2cf7a93ec3490c3ddda67624c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left\\langle x_{n_r}\\right\\rangle$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"38\" height=\"19\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/7/c17dd0a72cb06528993d591975faf08cf6288c63.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left\\langle x_n\\right\\rangle$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"32\" height=\"19\" /> which converges to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />. \n</p><p>As <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/c/8ecbd1ba3da8f2adef66a63f2ab32c47e63fa734.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[a,b]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> is closed, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/d/78d9dcd969a2c45f7cc9234aa1377b6ec1c2d5d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\in [a,b]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"66\" height=\"18\" />. Hence, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> is continous at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, and by the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Limit\" title=\"Limit\">sequential criterion for limits</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/3/4f34a913877fc54bb927d07f864f5f512ad44a1a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x_n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" /> is convergent, contradicting the assumption. \n</p><p>Similarly we can show that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> is bounded below\n</p><p>Now, Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/b/3bbce4c453e5dbd5353e06c8c6e58b2e0d592bf3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M=\\sup\\{f([a,b])\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"149\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>By the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Gap_lemma\" title=\"Gap lemma\">Gap lemma</a>, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/0/19061db16fe26d8408ebd6a4bfba2c869e85fc16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\forall n\\in\\mathbb{N}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"55\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/0/4701a1c9120a906e16506e9e474c479a452167e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\exists x_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/9/189564a2c28f9239c08e9c908153b9adbbd4e8a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M-f(x_n)&lt;\\frac{1}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"127\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>As <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/7/c17dd0a72cb06528993d591975faf08cf6288c63.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left\\langle x_n\\right\\rangle$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"32\" height=\"19\" /> is bounded, by <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Bolzano-Weierstrass_theorem\" title=\"Bolzano-Weierstrass theorem\">Bolzano-Weierstrass theorem</a>, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/7/c17dd0a72cb06528993d591975faf08cf6288c63.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left\\langle x_n\\right\\rangle$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"32\" height=\"19\" /> has a subsequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/2/3d242fcfc8b8d2cf7a93ec3490c3ddda67624c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left\\langle x_{n_r}\\right\\rangle$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"38\" height=\"19\" /> that converges to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/d/78d9dcd969a2c45f7cc9234aa1377b6ec1c2d5d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\in [a,b]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"66\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>As <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> is continous at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/9/459025e1c028e8b373a21d0a7e519a12b7737a14.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)\\in V_{\\frac{1}{n}}(M)\\forall n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"134\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>i.e. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f90cb68647535c6c1b11ca14ec316b0577b817f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)=M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"78\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"References\">References</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Maximum-minimum_theorem&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: References\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>R.G. Bartle, D.R. Sherbert, <i>Introduction to Real Analysis</i>, John Wiley &amp; Sons\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Maximum-minimum_theorem&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Calculus\" title=\"Calculus\">Calculus</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Bolzano%27s_theorem\" title=\"Bolzano&#39;s theorem\">Bolzano's theorem</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Closed_set\" title=\"Closed set\">Closed set</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Topology\" title=\"Topology\">Topology</a></li>\n</ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018095215\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.020 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.030 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 178/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 5885/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:6419:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018095215 and revision id 106020. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}